<title>JAPAN: Japan to computerise meat import paperwork.</title>
<headline>Japan to computerise meat import paperwork.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Agriculture Ministry said on Tuesday it will introduce a computerised system for dealing with documentation on meat imports, in a bid to speed up the procedure as the volume of such imports grows.</p>
<p>The new system, which will take effect from April 29, will enable local trade houses to submit documents on meat imports by personal computer, a ministry official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our quarantine procedure is taking more time, reflecting growing meat imports. The new system will make the procedure much more efficient,&quot; the ministry official said.</p>
<p>Local trade houses are currently obliged to submit papers both to quarantine stations and customs offices. But under the new system, they will be allowed to submit the documents via personal computers to a single computer network.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
